pr_body:
Fixes https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/issues/35851.

When looking up a `FieldInfo`, `ConstructorInfo`, or `MethodInfo` from a known handle, we'll now walk the cached member array _outside_ the critical section. If no match is seen, we'll fall back into the critical section code paths.

There's a race condition where another thread might be mutating the list at the same time we're reading from it. If this happens and we accidentally miss a matching entry, the fallback code which re-enters the critical section will detect this and do the right thing.

### Benchmark results

For single-threaded case, shows reduction in gen0 allocations per invocation. For multi-threaded case, shows reduction in lock contentions.

